  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through Saturday)\nIssued at 102 AM CDT SUN AUG 2 2026\n\nA cold front currently bisects the area, with convective coverage\nand intensity decreasing over the last hour. While brief\nlocalized intensification is possible as the front advances\ntoward the I-85 corridor by sunrise, the highest coverage\nprobability remains across southern areas from late morning\nthrough the afternoon. Concurrently, an upper low will traverse\nthe northern tier of the state, supporting scattered showers and\nisolated storms north of the  I-22/I-59 corridor. A developing\ndry slot between these features will yield improved conditions\nfor much of Central Alabama this afternoon.\n\nThe upper low will shear into a trough before reforming, leading\nto an unsettled pattern across the Southeast into early next\nweek, with the highest rain probabilities focused over the\neastern third of the forecast area. Heights will build by mid-\nweek, favoring a return to a diurnally driven summertime pattern.\n\n16",
